>", "docsize": 18451, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court", "author": "A Narendran", "authorEncoded": "a-narendran"}, {"tid": 7799023, "catids": null, "doctype": 1007, "publishdate": "2015-06-03", "authorid": 1358, "bench": [1358], "title": "Karuppannan vs The Superintendent Of Police on 3 June, 2015", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "final assessment order.\n \n \t3.3. As per  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>(4)  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, the presumption\nregarding the <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> could be made only ... wherein it is\nheld as follows:\n \n \t&quot;13. The proceeding under  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act is\nessentially a civil proceeding. The said provision", "docsize": 22439, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court", "author": "R Mahadevan", "authorEncoded": "r-mahadevan"}, {"tid": 59943156, "catids": [1], "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2011-09-09", "authorid": 1987, "bench": [1987], "title": "M/S Jtg Alloys Private Limited vs Punjab State Power Corporation Limited on 9 September, 2011", "numcites": 8, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "under  <b>Section</b>\n\n<b>126</b>(6) , Explanation (b), is reproduced hereunder:-\n \n             &quot;Explanation.-For the purposes of this <b>Section</b>,-\n\n              (a)   .........\n \n             (b) &quot; <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> ... <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> through a tampered meter which would\n\nconstitute a theft of <b>electricity</b> is still an &quot;unauthorized <b>use</b>&quot; of <b>electricity</b>\n\nunder  <b>Section</b>", "docsize": 21949, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Punjab-Haryana High Court", "author": "K Kannan", "authorEncoded": "k-kannan"}, {"tid": 129808390, "catids": null, "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2014-09-04", "authorid": 1795, "bench": [1795], "title": "Amar Singh & Anr vs Uttar Hry Bijli Vitran Nigam & Ors on 4 September, 2014", "numcites": 8, "numcit